From: Octavo (local foliate-js patch set)
Subject: [PATCH 0002] paginator: let the host set the portrait column count

The paginator takes `max-column-count` from an attribute, but when its
container is portrait it switches to the internal
`--_max-column-count-portrait` (1), which no attribute reaches. So a host
can't ask for two pages in a portrait area: on iPhone Duo the column count
would depend on the reader area's aspect ratio rather than on the fold.

Adds a `max-column-count-portrait` attribute that sets that property, the
same way `max-column-count` sets its own. Without the attribute nothing
changes.

Checked on the Duo simulator (spike 2b, docs/notes/duo-spreads.md): a
400x493 view with max-column-count=2 and max-inline-size=200px lays out
one column without this patch and two with it.

Applies on top of 0001. Apply from the repo root:
  git apply --directory=ReaderWeb/foliate-js ReaderWeb/foliate-js/patches/0002-portrait-column-count.patch
---
diff --git a/paginator.js b/paginator.js
index 309560d..dd6fa00 100644
--- a/paginator.js
+++ b/paginator.js
@@ -457,6 +457,7 @@ export class Paginator extends HTMLElement {
     static observedAttributes = [
         'flow', 'gap', 'margin',
         'max-inline-size', 'max-block-size', 'max-column-count',
+        'max-column-count-portrait',
     ]
     #root = this.attachShadow({ mode: 'closed' })
     #observer = new ResizeObserver(() => this.render())
@@ -666,6 +667,7 @@ export class Paginator extends HTMLElement {
             case 'margin':
             case 'max-block-size':
             case 'max-column-count':
+            case 'max-column-count-portrait':
                 this.#top.style.setProperty('--_' + name, value)
                 break
             case 'max-inline-size':
